    "lesson": {
      "title": "Two-piston hydraulic lift",
      "instruction": "How does a larger output piston trade force for travel?",
      "explanation": "Equal hydraulic head, massless frictionless pistons and incompressible fluid. Available force is a ceiling; a slow stroke uses exactly the balancing force. Below threshold both pistons remain fixed. Work is calculated using balancing load force, not the unused force ceiling. No pump/check-valve mechanism, leaks or acceleration."
